  "description": "One class per minimal API endpoint, discovered and mapped for you: implement IEndpoint<TGroup, TResponse> (a Map method holding a plain MapGet/MapPost chain) and IEndpointGroup (prefix, tags), call app.MapEndpoints(assemblies), and every endpoint is mapped into its group with its name, its success response from the handler's typed results, its error responses (401/403 whenever the endpoint ends up requiring authorization, 429 whenever it is rate limited, 413 for uploads, and ProducesErrors(...)), and AcceptsUpload/ProducesFile for file uploads and downloads. Endpoints are listed at compile time by a source generator and checked by an analyzer, so there is no assembly scan at startup and a broken endpoint (no group, two routes in Map, a handler that doesn't return TResponse) is a build error. Your own error schema (ProblemDetails by default), group and endpoint conventions for app-wide rules, and an extension point for request validation (see Hlibz.MinimalApi.Endpoints.FluentValidation).",
